---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout title="LibreTracks Privacy" description="Privacy information for LibreTracks optional usage statistics." lang="en">
  <main class="site-shell band legal-page">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h2>Optional usage statistics.</h2>
      <p>LibreTracks does not send usage data unless you explicitly allow it in the application.</p>
    </div>
    <section>
      <h3>What is collected</h3>
      <p>The application start and its UTC date and time; LibreTracks version, broad operating-system family, CPU architecture, device class and country; activation milestones such as create, open, import, play, save or export; use of closed feature categories; success or failure of selected actions; active-session milestones at 5, 15, 30 and 60 minutes; and broad installation-age and active-day ranges. Cloudflare infers the country from the network connection and LibreTracks stores only its two-letter code. A random secret remains only on the device; the app sends a pseudonymous derived token that changes each UTC day.</p>
      <h3>What is never collected</h3>
      <p>Project or session content, audio, song or file names, file paths, error messages, MIDI or audio hardware names, account information, advertising identifiers, serial numbers, IP addresses, cities, regions, coordinates and precise location. Events accept no free-text fields.</p>
      <h3>Purpose, legal basis and choices</h3>
      <p>The purpose is measuring activation, feature adoption, reliability, usage depth and trends, country-level geographic distribution, active versions and broad compatibility to inform product and business decisions. Processing is based on consent. Refusing has no effect on LibreTracks, and consent can be withdrawn at any time under Settings → General. Disabling statistics also removes the random local secret and coarse local counters.</p>
      <h3>Storage, publication and processor</h3>
      <p>Event rows are deleted after at most 90 days. The public dashboard contains general aggregates and hides countries, breakdowns and time buckets representing fewer than five devices. Detailed product metrics are shown only in an authenticated private dashboard. Cloudflare provides hosting, networking, country-level geolocation and database processing and necessarily handles network information such as an IP address transiently to provide those services; LibreTracks does not write that address or the full User-Agent into its telemetry database.</p>
      <h3>Your rights and contact</h3>
      <p>Because there is no account and the token changes daily, LibreTracks cannot normally associate a stored row with a person. You can stop future collection in the app. For privacy questions or rights requests, contact <a href="mailto:libretracks.app@gmail.com">libretracks.app@gmail.com</a>. You may also lodge a complaint with your local data-protection authority.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
